# Forestree's own runtime state. Regenerated as the app runs; never worth
# committing, and a source of constant merge conflicts if it is.
#
# The rest of this directory is your PROJECT's architecture — .config.forestree,
# checks.json, hooks.json, runbook.json — and IS meant to be committed.
#
# drift.json is committed ON PURPOSE: a finding stays in it until a human
# resolves or dismisses it, and the team shares that state through git. The
# scan bookkeeping that used to ride along inside it (when it last ran, at
# which commit) now lives in drift-scan-state.json, below, so a scan that
# finds nothing leaves drift.json untouched.
sessions/
debug/
tmp/
plugins/secrets.json
settings.local.json
planned-work.json
drift-scan-trace.json
drift-scan-state.json
config.json
